EXPERIMENT 20 – COMPARING SUMMARY REPORT AND AGGREGATE REPORT USING APACHE JMETER

AIM
To use Apache JMeter to compare the Summary Report and Aggregate Report listeners.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and create a Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 10, Ramp-up Period = 10 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add two HTTP Request samplers: GET / and GET /status_codes/404.
5. Add Summary Report, Aggregate Report and Graph Results listeners.
6. Run the plan and compare the report columns.
7. Identify the metrics available only in the Aggregate Report.
TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	10
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	10 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request 1	Name	Home
HTTP Request 1	Server Name	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	GET /
HTTP Request 2	Name	Status 404
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	GET /status_codes/404
Listeners	Added	Summary Report, Aggregate Report, Graph Results

INPUT
- Number of users: 10
- Loop count: 1
- Request 1: GET / (returns 200)
- Request 2: GET /status_codes/404 (returns 404)
- Total samples: \(10 \times 2 = 20\)
OUTPUT
Aggregate Report
Label	Samples	Error %
Home	10	0.00%
Status 404	10	100.00%
TOTAL	20	50.00%

Other report columns include Average, Median, 90% Line, 95% Line and 99% Line. Response times depend on the system and network.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to compare the Summary Report and Aggregate Report listeners, and the results were verified.
